<title>USA: Earthgrains doubles qtly div post-split.</title>
<headline>Earthgrains doubles qtly div post-split.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS, Mo. 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Earthgrains Co said Thursday its directors voted to double the company's quarterly dividend rate to $0.05 a share on a post-split basis.</p>
<p>The dividend is payable August 31 to shareholders of record on August 15.</p>
<p>The dividend will remain $0.05 a share but will effectively double because an already approved two-for-one stock split becomes effective July 28, record May 30.</p>
<p>Earthgrains is the third-largest producer of baked goods and the only manufacturer of store-brand canned refrigerated dough products in the U.S..</p>
<p>			((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
